  "summary": "This vibrant <b>Brazilian grilled skewer recipe</b> offers a delightful vegetarian centerpiece that highlights the distinctive texture of firm cheese combined with tender vegetables. The dish centers on traditional <b>queijo coalho</b>, a firm cheese that holds its shape beautifully over high heat without melting away. Paired with succulent chunks of <b>hearts of palm</b>, crisp bell peppers, and juicy cherry tomatoes, each skewer delivers a wonderful interplay of smoky, tangy, and savory flavors. A simple marinade of extra virgin olive oil, garlic, oregano, and fresh lime juice infuses the ingredients before they hit the flames, creating a charred crust and tender interior. Once grilled to golden perfection, the skewers are drizzled with zesty <b>chimichurri sauce</b> for an herbaceous finish that elevates every single bite. Perfect for outdoor gatherings or quick weeknight dinners, this colourful dish brings authentic tropical flair to your table without needing any meat. Serve alongside seasoned rice or a fresh green salad for a complete and satisfying meal.",
